{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>When the days are fulfilled.</b> The verb name [i.e., its form] is among possessors of alef, following the pattern of possessors of heh in the final position. And like it: לבלתי קראת לנו (Jeremiah 14:9, \"that You do not call to us\")." "<b>He shall bring him.</b> He shall bring himself [i.e., the nazirite himself], like וירעו הרועים אותם (Genesis 36:7–8, \"and the shepherds grazed them\" — the reflexive use of את). Or: the priest shall bring him, by command, against his will, to offer his sacrifice."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:16:37.496025124Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}